2.5️⃣ Security / Access Misconfiguration Incident

Storytelling answer:

“We once tightened IAM and RBAC policies as part of a least-privilege initiative. Shortly after the change,
deployments started 
failing and some services couldn’t access required resources.

The impact was limited but visible — health checks failed and new pods wouldn’t come up.

Logs showed authorization errors, confirming it was an access issue.

We rolled back the policy immediately to restore service, then carefully identified the missing permissions.

After the incident, we introduced staged permission testing, permission diff checks, and 
restricted access changes to defined change windows.

The learning was that security changes are high-risk and need the same rigor as production code changes.”
